: 'A Belarusian sprinter said Sunday that she was under the protection of the Japanese police after her country’s Olympic Committee tried, but failed, to forcibly send her home after she criticized her coaches for registering her for the wrong event.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Olympic Sprinter From Belarus Seeks Refuge in Japan, Fearing Jail at Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fearing Imprisonment at Home, Olympian From Belarus Seeks Protection in Japan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2020)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Olympic Committee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Timanovskaya, Kristina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-01T18:38:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Hopkins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hopkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b6a106b-0cef-5782-bc7a-340523d027ea', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b6a106b-0cef-5782-bc7a-340523d027ea'}, {'abstract': 'The rapper apologized on Monday after being criticized for asking fans at a performance to raise their phones in the air if they didn’t have H.I.V. or AIDS.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/01/arts/music/dababy-lollapalooza-canceled-homophobic-comments.html', 'snippet': 'The rapper apologized on Monday after being criticized for asking fans at a performance to raise their phones in the air if they didn’t have H.I.V. or AIDS.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day after DaBaby’s scheduled performance at the Lollapalooza music festival in Chicago was canceled, the promoters of events in New York and Las Vegas also announced new lineups that did not include the rapper, who apologized on Monday for making homophobic comments that have been condemned by other artists.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/01/multimedia/01xp-dababy2/merlin_191652117_e362718f-5349-413f-be8f-24ec6a460d38-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/01/multimedia/01xp-dababy2/merlin_191652117_e362718f-5349-413f-be8f-24ec6a460d38-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/01/multimedia/01xp-dababy2/merlin_191652117_e362718f-5349-413f-be8f-24ec6a460d38-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/01/multimedia/01xp-dababy2/merlin_191652117_e362718f-5349-413f-be8f-24ec6a460d38-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/01/multimedia/01xp-dababy2/merlin_191652117_e362718f-5349-413f-be8f-24ec6a460d38-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/01/multimedia/01xp-dababy2/merlin_191652117_e362718f-5349-413f-be8f-24ec6a460d38