, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/02/sports/02cover-1/02cover-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/02/sports/02cover-1/02cover-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/02/sports/02cover-1/02cover-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '东京奥运每日精彩瞬间：8月2日', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-08-03T02:27:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Universal', 'section_name': 'Universal', 'subsection_name': '中文', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/0ecc944e-0fac-5937-a5bb-37584492826c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/0ecc944e-0fac-5937-a5bb-37584492826c'}, {'abstract': 'Matchbook Distilling Company in Greenport, N.Y., is co-owned by a direct descendant of Hiram Walker, who created Canadian Club.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/02/dining/matchbook-distilling-company.html', 'snippet': 'Matchbook Distilling Company in Greenport, N.Y., is co-owned by a direct descendant of Hiram Walker, who created Canadian Club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sorted Fortune — a fragrant spirit made from heirloom musk melons grown on the North Fork of Long Island, with whey left over from White Moustache yogurt — is one of the latest products from Matchbook Distilling Company, in Greenport, N.Y. In the fall, a sunchoke spirit that suggests mezcal will be bottled for the second time. Leslie Merinoff, 34, co-founded this experimental distillery three years ago and comes to this business naturally; she’s a direct descendant of Hiram Walker, the 19th century American whiskey mogul and industrialist who worked in Canada and created Canadian Club. Hers is a small but diversified operation that gets ingredients like herbs and produce from nearby farms and food companies and turns them into limited runs of 30 to 500 bottles, often with poetic names. “Supporting local agriculture is what we do, and we’re having fun,” she said. Whiskey is made from mash using leftover bread from She Wolf Bakery in Brooklyn. Since most of the limited-run creations sell out fast, it pays to check the website.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-still/merlin_192097440_7ea8f6ed-44a6-434a-bc9f-8e963c9b997c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-still/merlin_192097440_7ea8f6ed-44a6-434a-bc9f-8e963c9b997c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-still/merlin_192097440_7ea8f6ed-44a6-434a-bc9f-8e963c9b997c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-still/merlin_192097440_7ea8f6ed-44a6-434a-bc9f-8e963c9b997c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1363, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-still/02burner-still-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-still/02burner-still-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-still/02burner-still-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Jewel of a Distillery With Storied Roots', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sip: This Distillery Comes With Storied Roots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcoholic Beverages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenport (Suffolk County, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-03T03:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c4a0a26-72ed-5a2a-80d5-974685885722', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c4a0a26-72ed-5a2a-80d5-974685885722'}, {'abstract': 'The auction house has added six European wines to its house label.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/02/dining/drinks/sothebys-wine-lo-stradone.html', 'snippet': 'The auction house has added six European wines to its house label.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sotheby’s, the auction house, sells wine collections, has its own wine store and, for the past two years, has also commissioned 13 well-made wines from France, Italy and California with its name on the labels. It has now expanded this in-house roster to include a rosé Champagne, a Provençal rosé, a Côtes du Rhône, a pinot grigio from Friuli, and two Tuscan reds: a well-made 2017 Chianti Rùfina produced by Frescobaldi; and Lo Stradone, a super Tuscan blend from the esteemed Ornellaia winery in the Maremma region. Like the original set, the wines are well priced, from $16.95 to $39.95. Lo Stradone, a rich, structured red, is an excellent introduction at $22.95 to super Tuscans, a category with wines that often sell for 10 times as much.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-wine/02burner-wine-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-wine/02burner-wine-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-wine/02burner-wine-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-wine/02burner-wine-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-wine/02burner-wine-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-wine/02burner-wine-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02burner-wine/02burner-wine-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Additions to the Sotheby’s Wine Collection', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Pour: Auction House Adds To Its Wine Holdings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-03T03:05:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c8b2859-0bf1-5a31-a1ab-3902df995cb9', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c8b2859-0bf1-5a31-a1ab-3902df995cb9'}, {'abstract': 'Tiwa Select is selling platters by a dozen artists with a dreamy presale viewing in a barn in the Catskills.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/02/dining/tiwa-select-big-plates.html', 'snippet': 'Tiwa Select is selling platters by a dozen artists with a dreamy presale viewing in a barn in the Catskills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tiwa Select, an online source for household and tabletop objects made by artists, is holding a live exhibit and sale called Big Plates, with serving platters from 13 artists commissioned by Alex Tieghi-Walker and Fiona Mackay, partners in the company. The platters, designed for summer entertaining, will be displayed in the woods near Ms. Mackay’s barn in Stone Ridge, N.Y., in the Catskills from Aug. 5 through 7 from 11 a.m. to 6 p.m. Confirmation of attendance must be made at studio@tiwa-select.com. The pieces, produced in small multiple editions, range in price from $420 to $3,800 each and will also be sold online.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/04BurnerPlate-2/02BurnerPlate-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/04BurnerPlate-2/02BurnerPlate-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/04BurnerPlate-2/02BurnerPlate-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/04BurnerPlate-2/02BurnerPlate-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/04BurnerPlate-2/02BurnerPlate-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/04BurnerPlate-2/02BurnerPlate-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/04BurnerPlate-2/02BurnerPlate-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Array of Tableware Up for Grabs', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To View: Array of Tableware Is Up for Grabs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Stone Ridge (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-03T03:09:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21d4f389-5d38-514c-b3e5-5a997ce74265', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21d4f389-5d38-514c-b3e5-5a997ce74265'}, {'abstract': 'Three instant versions from Cabot Cheese in Vermont make ample use of aged Cheddar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/02/dining/cabot-mac-and-cheese.html', 'snippet': 'Three instant versions from Cabot Cheese in Vermont make ample use of aged Cheddar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a fine cheese company produces its own mac and cheese, it pays to notice. Beecher’s Handmade Cheese and Murray’s Cheese are two of them. Now there’s Cabot Cheese, a Vermont-based cooperative of 800 farm families in the Northeast, known especially for its Cheddars. And it’s the aged Cheddar (dried and powdered) that’s included in the simple boxed mac and cheese made with organic shell pasta. Just add a little milk (they suggest low-fat but I used whole) and optional butter and it’s ready, creamy and flavorful, in about 20 minutes. The Seriously Sharp is just cheese, Bacon Cheddar has a smoky flavor but no visible meat and none among the ingredients, and Pepper Jack delivers some spice.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02Burner-Cabot/02Burner-Cabot-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/04/dining/02Burner-Cabot/02Burner-Cabot-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', '