', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e2b1356-7255-52c4-b84e-b930e07bf7d6', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e2b1356-7255-52c4-b84e-b930e07bf7d6'}, {'abstract': 'The hourslong raid, which killed eight people, targeted a top military official’s home near Kabul’s fortified green zone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/04/world/asia/afghanistan-kabul-taliban-attack.html', 'snippet': 'The hourslong raid, which killed eight people, targeted a top military official’s home near Kabul’s fortified green zone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The Taliban claimed responsibility on Wednesday for an attack on the home of a top military official in Kabul that killed eight people, highlighting the insurgents’ ability to strike in the heart of the Afghan capital as they continue their sweeping military campaign.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taliban Claim Responsibility for Major Attack in Afghan Capital', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taliban Claim Responsibility For Attack In Kabul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohammadi, Bismillah Khan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-04T12:16:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christina Goldbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christina', 'middlename': Non