rint_headline': 'Centrist Democrats See Series of Wins as Gut Check for Left', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Nina (1967- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Shontel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-04T23:22:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/619faacc-39cd-551a-b5fc-ee594f0fe663', 'word_count': 1356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/619faacc-39cd-551a-b5fc-ee594f0fe663'}, {'abstract': 'Progressives have not ruled out reopening the deal that senators are painstakingly putting together, and they do not intend to take it up for months, until after their other priorities are addressed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/04/us/politics/infrastructure-bill.html', 'snippet': 'Progressives have not ruled out reopening the deal that senators are painstakingly putting together, and they do not intend to take it up for months, until after their other priorities are addressed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As senators grind through votes this week on a $1 trillion bipartisan infrastructure bill, discontent about the legis