would be tragic if it became synonymous with a land of ex-soldiers for hire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take tens of thousands of former members of the military experienced in lethal tactics and skills, often provided by U.S. trainers. Give them meager pensions and little to do in an economy battered by the Covid-19 pandemic. Allow them — even encourage them — to sell their skills in a growing globalized market for security contractors and mercenaries.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/08/opinion/sunday/isacson_3/isacson_3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/08/opinion/sunday/isacson_3/isacson_3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 492}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/08/opinion/sunday/isacson_3/isacson_3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/08/opinion/sunday/isacson_3/isacson_3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1681, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/08/opinion/sunday/isacson_3/isacson_3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/08/opinion/sunday/isacson_3/isacson_3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/08/opinion/sunday/isacson_3/isacson_3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, '