s of mourning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/05/style/son-death-grief-social-qs.html', 'snippet': 'A reader asks for help dealing with pressure to put grief behind her after nine years of mourning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My son died nine years ago from an opioid overdose. He was bipolar and trying to get on with his life after college, but he hit a rough patch, made some poor choices and was gone. I have gotten grief counseling, and I’m better. The problem is my stepchildren. In the middle of celebrations of big events in their lives — weddings, births, job promotions — I am often seized with grief that my son is not there and will never be doing these things. My habit has been to leave the events quietly and let my husband spend happy times with the kids. But recently, my stepdaughter told me that my sudden absences are casting a pall over their lives. They think it’s time for me to move beyond my grief. I am confused and hurt by this. Advice?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/20/fashion/socialqs-2021-artwork/socialqs-2021-artwork-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/06/20/fashion/socialqs-2021-artwork/socialqs-2021-artwork-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/20/fashion/socialqs-2021-artwork/socialqs-2021-artwork-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/06/20/fashion/socialqs-2021-artwork/socialqs-2021-artwork-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1713, 'width': 1712, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo'