th': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/07/arts/05britney-update/05britney-update-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/07/arts/05britney-update/05britney-update-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/07/arts/05britney-update/05britney-update-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/07/arts/05britney-update/05britney-update-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/07/arts/05britney-update/05britney-update-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/07/arts/05britney-update/05britney-update-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Britney Spears Asks for Quick Hearing to Oust Her Father as Conservator', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britney Spears Asks for Speedier Hearing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wills and Estates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spears, Britney', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spears, Jamie (1952- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-05T19:21:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Day', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Day', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5eefddb9-0460-5032-a38f-3eec7aed3f8b', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5eefddb9-0460-5032-a38f-3eec7aed3f8b'}, {'abstract': 'The architect Christopher Rawlins moved into his Art Deco Manhattan building in 1999 and has used his space there as a laboratory for creating a sensual sort of Modernism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/05/t-magazine/an-elegant-inwood-apartment-designed-for-living-and-working.html', 'snippet': 'The architect Christopher Rawlins moved into his Art Deco Manhattan building in 1999 and has used his space there as a laboratory for creating a sensual sort of Modernism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One often hears that a home has “good bones.” The phrase is not typically applied to an entire neighborhood, but that’s exactly how the architect and historian Christopher Rawlins describes Manhattan’s Inwood, which, in addition to trains, parks and a vibrant immigrant presence, has one of the highest concentrations of Art Deco buildings in the United States, and is where he’s lived since 1999, when the area also appealed for its affordability. “You could practically reach into your pocket and pay cash for an apartment up here,” recalls Rawlins, who at the time was a few years out of graduate school and working at Alexander Gorlin Architects while also taking on the occasional teaching gig or independent commission. Today, he’s known for immortalizing the work of the 20th-century architect Horace Gifford with his 2013 book, “Fire Island Modernist,” and for his own reimaginings of midcentury styles and spaces — he recently completed a restoration of a late ’60s Harry Bates-designed home in Fire Island Pines. Moving uptown, says Rawlins, would allow him to reconceptualize his life. “I realized I didn’t have to be a cool kid in the Village and that, if I worked out of my home, I could call the shots professionally,” he says. And so he and his then-partner, the artist Tad Mike, purchased two units in the same 1935 cream brick co-op — a 700-square-foot one-bedroom to live in, and a 1,050-square-foot two-bedroom two floors below to use for their studios — and Rawlins launched his own practice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/05/t-magazine/design/Rawlins-slide-7FCC/Rawlins-slide-7FCC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/05/t-magazine/design/Rawlins-slide-7FCC/Rawlins-slide-7FCC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/05/t-magazine/design/Rawlins-slide-7FCC/Rawlins-slide-7FCC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/05/t-magazine/design/Rawlins-slide-7FCC/Rawlins-slide-7FCC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/05/t-magazine/design/Rawlins-slide-7FCC/Rawlins-slide-7FCC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/05/t-magazine/design/Rawlins-slide-7FCC/Rawlins-slide-7FCC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/05/t-magazine/design/Rawlins-slide-7FCC/Rawlins-slide-7FCC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Elegant Inwood Apartment Designed for Living and Working', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Repairs and Improvements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Inwood (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rawlins, Christopher', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Personal Profile', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-05T19:21:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Cumberbatch Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': 'Cumberbatch', 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faf9bcc9-84b9-5be6-891c-97ab32fe941f', 'word_count': 1457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faf9bcc9-84b9-5be6-891c-97ab32fe941f'}, {'abstract': 'An open letter from the group recommends that private companies, which employ 124 million Americans, require staff to get vaccinated, and offers guidance if they choose not to.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/05/us/politics/covid-vaccine-private-businesses.html', 'snippet': 'An open letter from the group recommends that private companies, which employ 124 million Americans, require staff to get vaccinated, and offers guidance if they choose not to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bipar