}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-06T16:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Climate', 'section_name': 'Climate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/505de163-dca1-5f2e-83e3-d78997d3e8ac', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/505de163-dca1-5f2e-83e3-d78997d3e8ac'}, {'abstract': 'Bonuses for winning Olympic medals can be as high as $740,000 for some athletes. Others have to be satisfied with a nice letter from the king.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/06/sports/olympics/olympics-medals-bonuses.html', 'snippet': 'Bonuses for winning Olympic medals can be as high as $740,000 for some athletes. Others have to be satisfied with a nice letter from the king.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — After winning a gold medal at the Summer Olympics here, the U.S. wrestler Tamyra Mensah-Stock had big plans for the bonus money that comes with it: buying her mother a $30,000 food truck.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/07/sports/07olympics-bonuses-mensahstock/merlin_192544275_7c65f4da-3342-4e92-b53d-d43bfe75e6c7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/07/sports/07olympics-bonuses-mensahstock/merlin_192544275_7c65f4da-3342-4e92-b53d-d43bfe75e6c7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/07/sports/07olympics-bonuses-mensahstock/merlin_192544275_7c65f4da-3342-