a8d28e234cc'}, {'abstract': 'It turns out that there is a bizarre absence of fully realized human beings in my sons’ fictional worlds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/06/opinion/boys-gender-books-culture.html', 'snippet': 'It turns out that there is a bizarre absence of fully realized human beings in my sons’ fictional worlds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A while back, at the bookstore with my three sons, I started flicking through a kids’ magazine that had the kind of hyper-pink sparkly cover that screams: “Boys! Even glancing in this direction will threaten your masculinity!”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/10/opinion/10whippman-inyt/30whippman_-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 564, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/10/opinion/10whippman-inyt/30whippman_-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 564}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/10/opinion/10whippman-inyt/30whippman_-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 963, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/10/opinion/10whippman-inyt/30whippman_-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1927, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/10/opinion/10whippman-inyt/30whippman_-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/10/opinion/10whippman-inyt/30whippman_-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/10/opinion/10whippman-inyt/30whippman_-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What We Are Not Teaching Boys About Being Human', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let’s Teach Boys the Art of Emotional Labor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '#MeToo Movement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-06T19:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth Whippman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Whippman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/55502ded-b2cf-5a24-aa52-40ea6973db46', 'word_count': 1335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55502ded-b2cf-5a24-aa52-40ea6973db46'}, {'abstract': "Family members of civil rights icon Medgar Evers and former Vice President Henry A. Wallace lament the filibuster in light of their loved ones' life and work.\xa0", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/06/opinion/voting-law-senate-civil-rights.html', 'snippet': "Family members of civil rights icon Medgar Evers and former Vice President Henry A. Wallace lament the filibuster in light of their loved ones' life and work.\xa0", 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m Myrlie Evers. Right before he was murdered, my husband, Medgar Evers, told me, “Don’t ever give up on those things that you believe in.” Medgar and I had a transcendent connection, and these words have lifted my spirits throughout the decades-long fight for justice against Medgar’s assassin, my time at the N.A.A.C.P. and my run for Congress against a far-right extremist. Now, those words guide me whenever I see things Medgar fought and died for being erased by misguided politicians.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/06/opinion/06Evers-Wallace/06Evers-Wallace-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/06/opinion/06Evers-Wallace/06Evers-Wallace-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/06/opinion/06Evers-Wallace/06Evers-Wallace-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/06/opinion/06Evers-Wallace/06Evers-Wallace-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/06/opinion/06Evers-Wallace/06Evers-Wallace-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/06/opinion/06Evers-Wallace/06Evers-Wallace-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/06/opinion/06Evers-Wallace/06Evers-Wallace-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Families Fought for Civil Rights. Don’t Let Jim Crow Stand.', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evers, Medgar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "New Deal (1930's)", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-06T19:03:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Myrlie Evers and Henry Scott Wallace', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Myrlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Evers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': 'Scott', 'lastname': 'Wallace', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/98944577-9c2f-5994-9e74-7e0653468270', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98944577-9c2f-5994-9e74-7e0653468270'}, {'abstract': 'While such measures have prompted protests in France and divided Americans, Italians are enjoying a season of rationality under Prime Minister Mario Draghi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/06/world/europe/italy-green-pass-vaccination-covid.html', 'snippet': 'While such measures have prompted protests in France and divided Americans, Italians are enjoying a season of rationality under Prime Minister Mario Draghi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORBETELLO, Italy — On Friday, the first day that Italians needed to present a nationwide health passport for access to indoor dining, museums, gyms, theaters and a wide range of social activities, Margherita Catenuto, 18, from Sicily, proudly showed a bar code at the Capitoline Museum in Rome certifying that she was vaccinated.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/06/world/06Italy-VaccinePassport01/merlin_192855414_a04540a1-621d-43af-928a-61463fb43570-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/06/world/06Italy-VaccinePassport01/merlin_192855414_a04540a1-621d-43af-928a-61463fb43570-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/06/world/06Italy-VaccinePassport01/merlin_192855414_a04540a1-621d-43af-928a-61463fb43570-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/06/world/06Italy-VaccinePassport01/merlin_192855414_a04540a1-621d-43af-928a-61463fb43570-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1355, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/06/world/06Italy-VaccinePassport01/merlin_192855414_a04540a1-621d-43af-928a-61463fb43570-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/06/world/06Italy-VaccinePassport01/merlin_192855414_a04540a1-621d-43af-928a-61463fb43570-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75,