11th medal made her the most decorated American track-and-field athlete in Olympic history, surpassing Carl Lewis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Allyson Felix had made her mark, collecting so many titles and winning so many races as the most celebrated female athlete in American track and field. By Saturday night, her accomplishments were officially unparalleled in U.S. track, and she found herself in a familiar position at Olympic Stadium: atop the podium with a gold medal draped around her neck.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/sports/07olympics-allyson-felix-tokyo-1-sub/merlin_193001508_1a5957c8-0861-4f51-a3c4-eb163a2da6cb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/07/sports/07olympics-allyson-felix-tokyo-1-sub/merlin_193001508_1a5957c8-0861-4f51-a3c4-eb163a2da6cb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/sports/07olympics-allyson-felix-tokyo-1-sub/merlin_193001508_1a5957c8-0861-4f51-a3c4-eb163a2da6cb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/sports/07olympics-allyson-felix-tokyo-1-sub/merlin_193001508_1a5957c8-0861-4f51-a3c4-eb163a2da6cb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/sports/07olympics-allyson-felix-tokyo-1-sub/merlin_193001508_1a5957c8-0861-4f51-a3c4-eb163a2da6cb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'th