', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dbbd8fd-c0b9-5746-b382-6ec6658edec4', 'word_count': 1812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dbbd8fd-c0b9-5746-b382-6ec6658edec4'}, {'abstract': 'Young undocumented immigrants have waited long enough to plan their lives.\xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/09/opinion/daca-dreamers-citizenship.html', 'snippet': 'Young undocumented immigrants have waited long enough to plan their lives.\xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'We were each 10 when our families — Lorella’s from Peru, Hina’s from Pakistan — moved with us to the United States. Our parents arrived here determined to find the best medical care. For Hina’s sister Aleeza, America meant treatment for a life-threatening brain condition that doctors in Dubai and India warned was available nowhere else. For Lorella, whose right leg was amputated after a car accident in Peru, the United States held the promise of advanced prosthetics and a country where she could thrive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/11/opinion/11PraeliNaveed-inyt/09PraeliNaveed-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/11/opinion/11PraeliNaveed-inyt/09PraeliNaveed-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/11/opinion/11PraeliNaveed-inyt/09PraeliNaveed-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/11/opinion/11PraeliNaveed-inyt/09PraeliNaveed-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, '