ject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Jobs Plan (2021)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-09T22:56:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Cochrane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cochrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a945278e-2735-54d9-b3ad-379eebe69b81', 'word_count': 1730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a945278e-2735-54d9-b3ad-379eebe69b81'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not as bad as you thought. It’s worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/09/opinion/climate-denial-covid-denial.html', 'snippet': 'It’s not as bad as you thought. It’s worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before the right embraced Covid denial, there was climate denial. Many of the attitudes that have characterized the right-wing response to the coronavirus pandemic — refusal to acknowledge facts, accusations that scientists are part of a vast liberal conspiracy, refusal to address the crisis — were foreshadowed in the climate debate.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/11/opinion/11krugman-lead-inyt/09krugman-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/11/opinion/11krugman-lead-inyt/09krugman-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/11/opinion/11krugman-lead-inyt/09krugman-lead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/11/opinion/11krugman-lead-inyt/09krugman-lead-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/11/opinion/11krugman-lead-inyt/09krugman-lead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/11/opinion/11krugman-lead-inyt/09krugman-lead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/11/opinion/11krugman-lead-inyt/09krugman-lead-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate Denial, Covid Denial and the Right’s Descent', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Covid Denial And the Right’s Descent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rumors and Misinformation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Right-Wing Extremism and Alt-Right', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-09T23:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2243ebf-984b-59bf-8856-57895050fd3a', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2243ebf-984b-59bf-8856-57895050fd3a'}, {'abstract': 'Methane is yet another obstacle in the path to combating climate change.\xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/09/opinion/climate-crisis-carbon-dioxide.html', 'snippet': 'Methane is yet another obstacle in the path to combating climate change.\xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'In conversations around the climate crisis, there’s often a focus on carbon dioxide. It is trapping heat and warming our atmosphere, fueling deadlier climate disasters than normal and costing billions year after year. We are right to focus on carbon dioxide. In 2019, it made up about 80 percent of human-caused, heat-trapping pollution in the United States. Reducing it remains the key to achieving as soon as possible a net-zero economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/opinion/12Castor-inyt/merlin_175641603_db1a8047-ada0-4fb5-826a-048bccf357a1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/12/opinion/12Castor-inyt/merlin_175641603_db1a8047-ada0-4fb5-826a-048bccf357a1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/opinion/12Castor-inyt/merlin_175641603_db1a8047-ada0-4fb5-826a-048bccf357a1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/opinion/12Castor-inyt/merlin_175641603_db1a8047-ada0-4fb5-826a-048bccf357a1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/opinion/12Castor-inyt/merlin_175641603_db1a8047-ada0-4fb5-826a-048bccf357a1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/12/opinion/12Castor-inyt/merlin_175641603_db1a8047-ada0-4fb5-826a-048bccf357a1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/opinion/12Castor-inyt/merlin_175641603_db1a8047-ada0-4fb5-826a-048bccf357a1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main'