.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The heat of the day can be deadly,” says Lilia Menconi, the author of a guidebook for hiking in and around Phoenix, where temperatures have already reached 118 degrees this summer. Skip walking in the midday sun and start your hike at dusk instead, when a cooler world opens up around you. “You can hear coyotes and see scorpions and bats and all kinds of nocturnal animals,” says Menconi, who sometimes brings along a black light that makes scorpions glow blue-green in the dark.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-tip/15mag-tip-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-tip/15mag-tip-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-tip/15mag-tip-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-tip/15mag-tip-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-tip/15mag-tip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-tip/15mag-tip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-tip/15mag-tip-thumbLarge.jpg', 'he