hapiro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ac964a1-9bfc-5afb-96f6-d3c5dcb8667f', 'word_count': 1362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ac964a1-9bfc-5afb-96f6-d3c5dcb8667f'}, {'abstract': 'What does love look like? This intimate short film captures the relationship between the artist Wilfrid Wood and his boyfriend-muse, Theo Adamson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/10/opinion/drawings-of-my-bf-love.html', 'snippet': 'What does love look like? This intimate short film captures the relationship between the artist Wilfrid Wood and his boyfriend-muse, Theo Adamson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wilfrid Wood has been drawing his boyfriend and muse, Theo Adamson, since 2016. The resulting pictures — Mr. Adamson posing provocatively, snoring on the sofa, picking his nose — were brought together for Mr. Wood’s show “Drawings of My BF” in 2019. As I stood among these portraits, I realized I was seeing Mr. Adamson in a way I’d experienced only with my ex-boyfriend in our quieter moments of intimate togetherness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/02/opinion/opdoc-drawingsofmybf/opdoc-drawingsofmybf-articleLarge.png', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/02/opinion/opdoc-drawingsofmybf/opdoc-drawingsofmybf-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/02/opinion/opdoc-drawingsofmybf/opdoc-drawingsofmybf-jumbo.png', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/02/opinion/opdoc-drawingsofmybf/opdoc-drawingsofmybf-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1440, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/02/opinion/opdoc-drawingsofmybf/opdoc-drawingsofmybf-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/02/opinion/opdoc-drawingsofmybf/opdoc-drawingsofmybf-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/02/opinion/opdoc-drawingsofmybf/opdoc-drawingsofmybf-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love Means Drawing Your Boyfriend 1,000 Times', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wood, Wilfrid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-10T09:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/be3ccb3d-8ce1-59c0-8a3f-ea9a477c6fb3', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be3ccb3d-8ce1-59c0-8a3f-ea9a477c6fb3'}, {'abstract': 'Frustrations grew behind the scenes among top leaders on both sides, poten