ghanistan, the group is seizing control of cities. Why is it succeeding so quickly?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend, after months of fighting, the Taliban made a huge breakthrough in their bid to take control of Afghanistan, seizing several cities and suddenly claiming a lot of the north.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Taliban’s Advance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gall, Carlotta', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'audio-neutral-informative', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-10T10:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Podcasts', 'section_name': 'Podcasts', 'subsection_name': 'The Daily', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise, Luke Vander Ploeg, Lynsea Garrison, Sydney Harper, Eric Krupke, Clare Toeniskoetter, M.J. Davis Lin, Marion Lozano and Chris Wood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Luke', 'middlename': 'Vander', 'lastname': 'Ploeg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Lynsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krupke', 'qualifier': 