You’d think the idea that humans can modify the weather would be exciting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/11/magazine/rain-dubai.html', 'snippet': 'You’d think the idea that humans can modify the weather would be exciting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Driving coastward through Mississippi last month, I hit rain. First it spat at the windshield, a few drops sprinkling down from the sky onto a 2009 Accord. Then the bucket tipped, the road disappearing into smudges of light and water cascading on glass in the milliseconds between frantic wiper swipes. I eased into a doughnut shop’s flooded parking lot and settled in to watch.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-screenland/15mag-screenland-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-screenland/15mag-screenland-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-screenland/15mag-screenland-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-screenland/15mag-screenland-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-screenland/15mag-screenland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-screenland/15mag-screenland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15mag-screenland/15mag-screenland-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Did They Really Make It Rain Over Dubai? Does It Matter?', 'kicker': 'Screenland', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dark Clouds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deserts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dubai (United Arab Emirates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United Arab Emirates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-11T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul McAdory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McAdory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08c6c9a8-4a1b-55fd-833d-4cad8b638667', 'word_count': 1217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08c6c9a8-4a1b-55fd-833d-4cad8b638667'}, {'abstract': 'Employers everywhere are deploying D.E.I. programs to be less racist. But do they even work?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/11/opinion/workplace-diversity-dei-initiative.html', 'snippet': 'Employers everywhere are deploying D.E.I. programs to be less racist. But do they even work?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s time to rethink what’s working in the modern workplace and what’s failing. Amid a pandemic that overturned how so many work, increased calls for racial and social justice put a new pressure on companies to ensure — or at least to seem as if they ensure — equality among their employees. Diversity, equity and inclusion (D.E.I.) programs are an increasingly popular solution deployed by management. But do these initiatives do marginalized employees any good? And who are the true beneficiaries of diversity programs, anyway?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Workplace Diversity Programs Doing More Harm Than Good?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'audio-neutral-informative', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-11T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By ‘The Argument'", 'person': [], 'organization': "The Argument'"}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a40c0bd-8c42-543b-bf92-331956f91f21', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a40c0bd-8c42-543b-bf92-331956f91f21'}, {'abstract': 'High-intensity interval training has surprising benefits for fitness and physical power, but don’t stay seated the rest of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/11/well/move/exercise-high-intensity-interval-training-hiit.html', 'snippet': 'High-intensity interval training has surprising benefits for fitness and physical power, but don’t stay seated the rest of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A mere four seconds of all-out exercise, repeated two or three dozen times, could be all many of us need to build and maintain our fitness, strength and physical power, according to an inspiring new study of the potency of super-quick workouts. The findings expand on other, recent studies showing that four-second interval workouts beneficially affect metabolism and muscles in adults of various ages. But they may also highlight new concerns about what we miss if we make our workouts too brief.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/17/well/physed-stairs/merlin_19258077_be54f9a1-a0a5-42b6-9f1b-0099a4901feb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/17/well/physed-stairs/merlin_19258077_be54f9a1-a0a5-42b6-9f1b-0099a4901feb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/17/well/physed-stairs/merlin_19258077_be54f9a1-a0a5-42b6-9f1b-0099a4901feb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/17/well/physed-stairs/merlin_19258077_be54f9a1-a0a5-42b6-9f1b-0099a4901feb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/17/well/physed-stairs/merlin_19258077_be54f9a1-a0a5-42b6-9f1b-0099a4901feb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/17/well/physed-stairs/merlin_19258077_be54f9a1-a0a5-42b6-9f1b-0099a4901feb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/17/well/physed-stairs/merlin_19258077_be54f9a1-a0a5-42b6-9f1b-0099a4901feb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exercise Vigorously for 4 Seconds. Repeat. Your Muscles May Thank You.', 'kicker': 'Phys Ed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stronger Bodies, 4 Seconds at a Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Medicine & Science in Sports & Exercise (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-11T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Move', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65b3dd8d-600e-5a82-8d49-ae03250e043f', 'word_count': 881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65b3dd8d-600e-5a82-8d49-ae03250e043f'}, {'abstract': 'Parents need time alone, but how do I explain that to my tween?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/11/parenting/parents-alone-time-pandemic.html', 'snippet': 'Parents need time alone, but how do I explain that to my tween?', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the best days of 2020 for me was in December when I got a root canal. I got to be horizontal in the dentist’s chair without the ability to doomscroll or anyone asking me for fruit snacks. Afterward, since I’d already told my family and colleagues I’d be gone a while, I wandered around downtown Manhattan, bought a $6 latte, browsed used books on the sidewalk and listened to a grown-up podcast as I drove home.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/10/well/00well-time-alone-nl/00well-time-alone-nl-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/10/well/00well-time-alone-nl/00well-time-alone-nl-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/10/well/00well-time-alone-nl/00well-time-alone-nl-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/10/well/00well-time-alone-nl/00well-time-alone-nl-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/10/well/00well-time-alone-nl/00well-time-alone-nl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/10/well/00well-time-alone-nl/00well-time-alone-nl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/10/well/00well-time-alone-nl/00well-time-alone-nl-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I Need to Hide From My Kids', 'kicker': 'The NYT Parenting Newsletter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Here to Help; How Parents Can Get Alone Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-11T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Parenting', 'section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farah Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b510c38-ae3d-526b-af2c-24d139fc50e1', 'word_count': 1062, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b510c38-ae3d-526b-af2c-24d139fc50e1'}, {'abstract': 'One in five parents of children age 12 to 17 said their child would “definitely not” get vaccinated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/11/us/politics/school-mask-mandate.html', 'snippet': 'One in five parents of children age 12 to 17 said their child would “definitely not” get vaccinated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American parents of school-age children are more supportive of school mask requirements than mandatory coronavirus vaccines, according to a new survey. It found that nearly two-thirds of those parents want schools to insist on masks for students, teachers and staff members who do not have their shots.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/11/world/11virus-briefing-kidsvaccine/merlin_185301561_1c83526e-f41e-4aaf-ab7b-ba25c2995e52-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/11/world/11virus-briefing-kidsvaccine/merlin_185301561_1c83526e-f41e-4aaf-ab7b-ba25c2995e52-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400