ticle', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65778550-aca8-5aa8-b685-ca3ce59573a0', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65778550-aca8-5aa8-b685-ca3ce59573a0'}, {'abstract': 'As a doctor who cares for the dying, I know that\xa0direct-care aides are invaluable to patients and their families. We need to honor the work they do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/11/opinion/health-care-aides-elderly.html', 'snippet': 'As a doctor who cares for the dying, I know that\xa0direct-care aides are invaluable to patients and their families. We need to honor the work they do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While I slept in my home, my mother lay dying on the bathroom floor in her home in another state. She was not alone. Her longtime professional home health aide was by her side, propping her up with a hastily grabbed pillow and holding her hand.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/sunday-review/11hallarman_2/11hallarman_2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/15/sunday-review/11hallarman_2/11hallarman_2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/sunday-review/11hallarman_2/11hallarman_2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/sunday-revi