r Molly Seidel is the latest athlete to win by prioritizing self care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/11/opinion/molly-seidel-simone-biles-olympics.html', 'snippet': 'The medal-winning marathoner Molly Seidel is the latest athlete to win by prioritizing self care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The marathoner Molly Seidel has always been a formidable athlete, but her ascent to the Olympic medal podium was not linear. She skipped the 2016 U.S. Olympic trials to check into treatment for obsessive-compulsive disorder, depression, anxiety and disordered eating.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/opinion/13crouse-inyt/11crouse-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/13/opinion/13crouse-inyt/11crouse-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/opinion/13crouse-inyt/11crouse-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/opinion/13crouse-inyt/11crouse-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1547, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/opinion/13crouse-inyt/11crouse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/13/opinion/13crouse-inyt/11crouse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/opinion/13crouse-inyt/11crouse-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Be Afraid to Quit. It Could Help You Win.', 'kicker': 'Lindsay crouse', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seidel, Molly (1994- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2020)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biles, Simone', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-11T09:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/13a34f78-66db-55f2-869e-73c21db3b892', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13a34f78-66db-55f2-869e-73c21db3b892'}, {'abstract': 'Her eye chart tests showed improvement. It took a radical experiment to find out why her reality wasn’t matching up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/11/magazine/glaucoma-bak.html', 'snippet': 'Her eye chart tests showed improvement. It took a radical experiment to find out why her reality wasn’t matching up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The burning started as soon as the 59-year-old woman put the drops into her eye. She blinked to try to rinse away the medication with her tears. She leaned forward to the mirror. Her left eye was red and angry-looking. She’d been using these eye drops for nearly a year to treat her newly diagnosed glaucoma, adding artificial tears for the dry eyes that appeared a few months later. And while she’d had plenty of problems with her eyes since all this started, this fiery pain was new. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Diagnosis_1/15Diagnosis_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 468, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Diagnosis_1/15Diagnosis_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 468}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Diagnosis_1/15Diagnosis_1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Diagnosis_1/15Diagnosis_1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1560, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Diagnosis_1/15Diagnosis_1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Diagnosis_1/15Diagnosis_1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Diagnosis_1/15Diagnosis_1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eye Drops Were Supposed to Help Her Vision. Why Did It Feel Worse?', 'kicker': 'Diagnosis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eye Drops Were Supposed to Help Her Vision. Why Did It Feel Worse?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyes and Eyesight', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glaucoma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cataracts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Drug Use)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-11T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e203a45-7c94-5491-8768-58aa8d64266f', 'word_count': 1468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e203a45-7c94-5491-8768-58aa8d64266f'}, {'abstract': 'The Taliban seized nine cities over six days in a major escalation of their military offensive. Here’s what you need to know.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/11/world/asia/taliban-afghanistan-troops-explainer.html', 'snippet': 'The Taliban seized nine cities over six days in a major escalation of their military offensive. Here’s what you need to know.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Since international troops began withdrawing from Afghanistan in May, the Taliban have carried out a sweeping military campaign and gained control of much of the country’s rural areas. But for months, the insurgents failed to capture major cities — until now.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/11/world/11afghanistan-explainer/merlin_192879819_4e6197c2-6710-4f24-8680-a125e6f255be-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType':