et', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2020)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '3-D Devices and Effects', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker-Pope, Tara', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Marcell (1994- )', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-11T09:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Times Insider', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Bures', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bures', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f55639a-da0c-5ca6-83d0-da41aad3200c', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f55639a-da0c-5ca6-83d0-da41aad3200c'}, {'abstract': 'It seemed like an easy crime to stop:  protected Indonesian rainforest, cut for coffee farms. But a globalized economy can undermine even the best-laid plans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/11/magazine/indonesia-rainforest-coffee.html', 'snippet': 'It seemed like an easy crime to stop:  protected Indonesian rainforest, cut for coffee farms. But a globalized economy can undermine even the best-laid plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the fall of 2015, Matt Leggett, a newly hired senior adviser for the Wildlife Conservation Society, found himself sitting in a meeting in Jakarta, Indonesia, wondering if someone had missed the point. The meeting, as he remembers it, was meant to unveil some good news about tigers. In brief: Back in 2002, a survey of one of the last habitats of the critically endangered Sumatran tiger, Bukit Barisan Selatan National Park, showed a tiger population that, in biologist-speak, amounted to only\xa01.6 tigers per 100 square kilometers. He learned of a significant improvement: 2.8 tigers per 100 square kilometers. Here was statistical proof that their approach — a collaboration with the Indonesian government to infiltrate poaching networks and prevent a cycle of livestock deaths and revenge killings — had been effective. Tiger numbers were going up. Conservation was working the way it should. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Coffee_image1/15Coffee_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Coffee_image1/15Coffee_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Coffee_image1/15Coffee_image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Coffee_image1/15Coffee_image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1264, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Coffee_image1/15Coffee_image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/15/magazine/15Coffee_image1/15Coffee_image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 