ence', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Anthes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anthes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2cb44cc-0423-5288-9408-9b8941aee045', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2cb44cc-0423-5288-9408-9b8941aee045'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian’s “Milk and Money Tour” hits the Beacon Theater at an uncertain time for live comedy. Luckily, the sex jokes are her funniest yet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/11/arts/ali-wong-beacon-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The comedian’s “Milk and Money Tour” hits the Beacon Theater at an uncertain time for live comedy. Luckily, the sex jokes are her funniest yet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the raucous first performance of her new show at the Beacon Theater on Tuesday, Ali Wong bemoaned the state of male groupies, compared oral sex to a pepper grinder and advised women to make stuff up when talking dirty. “The lies,” she says, adopting a hint of the voice of a preacher, “will set you free.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/arts/11comedy-wong1/11comedy-wong1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/12/arts/11comedy-wong1/11comedy-wong1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/arts/11comedy-wong1/11comedy-wong1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/arts/11comedy-wo