medy and Humor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-12T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Hodgman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodgman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29c77393-3d76-54fc-8af7-f6ab0582d6a9', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29c77393-3d76-54fc-8af7-f6ab0582d6a9'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Cuomo inherited his father’s fierce competitive spirit but not his humanity or introspection.\xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/12/opinion/andrew-cuomo-mario-resignation.html', 'snippet': 'Andrew Cuomo inherited his father’s fierce competitive spirit but not his humanity or introspection.\xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I knew Andrew Cuomo, he was the 20-something top adviser to the governor he called Mario, and I was the 20-something Albany bureau chief for Newsday. I still remember how he ended our occasional phone calls: “Bye, hon,” hanging up immediately before I could protest. It was vintage Andrew — calculated and patronizing, a show of power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/14/opinion/14pawel_print/merlin_75214585_6a22370e-6cf4-423f-9fab-3d3a4f83ca79-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/14/opinion/14pawel_print/merlin_75214585_6a22370e-6cf4-423f-9fab-3d3a4f83ca79-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/14/opinion/14pawel_print/merlin_75214585_6a22370e-6cf4-423f-9fab-3d3a4f83ca79-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/14/opinion/14pawel_print/merlin_75214585_6a22370e-6cf4-423f-9fab-3d3a4f83ca79-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/14/opinion/14pawel_print/merlin_75214585_6a22370e-6cf4-423f-9fab-3d3a4f83ca79-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/14/opinion/14pawel_print/merlin_75214585_6a22370e-6cf4-423f-9fab-3d3a4f83ca79-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/14/opinion/14pawel_print/merlin_75214585_6a22370e-6cf4-423f-9fab-3d3a4f83ca79-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Is How a Political Dynasty Bites the Dust', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Slow Death of a Political Dynasty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Mario M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Hazards and Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-12T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'