ws', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f27680f-5a78-5688-97de-f85995adc780', 'word_count': 2016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f27680f-5a78-5688-97de-f85995adc780'}, {'abstract': 'A first look inside the camp where more than 1,000 migrants are being quarantined after testing positive for the virus. At least 1,000 others are also under isolation after positive Covid tests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/12/us/coronavirus-migrants-border-covid.html', 'snippet': 'A first look inside the camp where more than 1,000 migrants are being quarantined after testing positive for the virus. At least 1,000 others are also under isolation after positive Covid tests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MISSION, Texas — On the edge of the Rio Grande in South Texas, sprawling Anzalduas Park has long been a popular spot for bird-watching, family cookouts and fishing. But earlier this month, the grassland expanse with barbecue grills and picnic tables was put off-limits, transformed into a large Covid-19 quarantine camp for migrants who have crossed from Mexico.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/us/12virus-border-1/merlin_193138515_c7c99a07-2d2c-40ea-9dc1-0e3cc3209639-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/12/us/12virus-border-1/merlin_193138515_c7c99a07-2d2c-40ea-9dc1-0e3cc3209639-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/us/12virus-border-1/merlin_193138515_c7c99a07-2d2c-40ea-9dc1-0e3cc3209639-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/us/12virus-border