, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a23e1a3a-f731-556e-afc2-9aa7471177e1', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a23e1a3a-f731-556e-afc2-9aa7471177e1'}, {'abstract': 'Four unrelated women with serious emotional baggage are connected by an incident on the subway in this indie drama directed by David Gutnik.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/12/movies/materna-review.html', 'snippet': 'Four unrelated women with serious emotional baggage are connected by an incident on the subway in this indie drama directed by David Gutnik.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Materna,” the debut feature by David Gutnik, four anguished New York women are connected by an incident on the subway involving — surprise, surprise — an unhinged man (Sturgill Simpson). Subtler and more focused than cloyingly grandiose interlocking dramas like “Crash,” it takes an interest — as the title suggests — in motherhood and mothering: the anxieties related to pregnancy and child-rearing; the guilt and frustrations born of generational rifts.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/arts/12materna/merlin_192802569_47817c9f-52fe-4ca5-b25b-4c7ba8a92e1d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/13/arts/12materna/merlin_192802569_47817c9f-52fe-4ca5-b25b-4c7ba8a92e1d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 322}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/arts/12materna/merlin_192802569_47817c9f-52fe-4ca5-b25b-4c7ba8a92e1d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/arts/12materna/merlin_192802569_47817c9f-52fe-4ca5-b25b-4c7ba8a92e1d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1099, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/arts/12materna/12materna-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/13/arts/12materna/12materna-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/arts/12materna/12materna-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Materna’ Review: Mommy Issues', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Materna', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Materna (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gutnik, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-12T11:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beatrice Loayza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beatrice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Loayza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/39cef6b8-b366-57ee-bcac-de6f30b99b63', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39cef6b8-b366-57ee-bcac-de6f30b99b63'}, {'abstract': 'This documentary from Peter Nicks follows Oakland High School seniors as they fight for social justice and face Covid-19 on their way to graduation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/12/movies/homeroom-review.html', 'snippet': 'This documentary from Peter Nicks follows Oakland High School seniors as they fight for social justice and face Covid-19 on their way to graduation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On their first day of school in 2019, members of the senior class at Oakland High School in Oakland, Calif., looked forward to Instagram posts and a year of tuning out teachers who drone on about math and classroom rules. More engaged classmates, like Denilson Garibo, a student governing board representative, might have anticipated that the year would include social justice organizing. But it would have been hard for the class of 2020 to predict the changes that the Covid-19 pandemic and the George Floyd protests would bring to their lives. This unprecedented year is captured in vérité style in the heartfelt documentary “Homeroom.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/arts/12homeroom-art/12homeroom-art-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/12/arts/12homeroom-art/12homeroom-art-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/arts/12homeroom-art/12homeroom-art-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/arts/12homeroom-art/12homeroom-art-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/arts/12homeroom-art/12homeroom-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name'