'lead_paragraph': 'In the past month, the Delta variant has driven up the number of new Covid cases by tens of thousands, thrown America’s pandemic response back into chaos and jeopardized the nation’s fragile economic recovery. In light of this, you might think that all of us — Republicans and Democrats alike — could at least agree on one thing: A well-functioning democratic society requires, at a bare minimum, public officials competent enough to tackle the numerous challenges we face.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/sunday/18Brooks/18Brooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/sunday/18Brooks/18Brooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/sunday/18Brooks/18Brooks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/sunday/18Brooks/18Brooks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/sunday/18Brooks/18Brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/sunday/18Brooks/18Brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/sunday/18Brooks/18Brooks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Competence Is Critical for Democracy. Let’s Redefine It.', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Do We Hate Competence?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democracy (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-15T14:15:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosa Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/edfa9679-3cb3-55c5-bd1f-49b10709661f', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edfa9679-3cb3-55c5-bd1f-49b10709661f'}, {'abstract': 'Excessive use of force is common in Brazil, and most of the targets of that violence are Black youths in the favelas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/15/opinion/international-world/brazil-blacks-police-brutality.html', 'snippet': 'Excessive use of force is common in Brazil, and most of the targets of that violence are Black youths in the favelas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — In 2015, Adriana Perez da Silva’s 16-year-old son and four of his friends were driving home after a day in the park when the police fired at their car, killing them. Ms. Silva believes they were targeted because they were Black. As a researcher of police abuses in Latin America at Human Rights Watch, I have interviewed many survivors and relatives of victims. But her interview has stayed with me.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/16/opinion/16munoz-acebes1/00munoz-acebes1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/16/opinion/16munoz-acebes1/00munoz-acebes1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/16/opinion/16munoz-acebes1/00munoz-acebes1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/16/opinion/16munoz-acebes1/00munoz-acebes1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/16/opinion/16munoz-acebes1/00munoz-acebes1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/16/opinion/16munoz-acebes1/00munoz-acebes1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/16/opinion/16munoz-acebes1/00munoz-acebes1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Rio, a Cautionary Tale on Police Violence', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Rio, a Cautionary Tale on Police Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Reform', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-15T14:15:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Opinion | The World', 'byline': {'original': 'By César Muñoz Acebes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'César', 'middlename': 'Muñoz', 'lastname': 'Acebes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9f8ed4d-f88a-5011-9223-bab6cb0c6d92', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9f8ed4d-f88a-5011-9223-bab6cb0c6d92'}, {'abstract': 'The popular tourist destination is now in the top 20 U.S. states and territories for cases per capita, according to a New York Times database.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/15/us/us-virgin-islands-covid-surge.html', 'snippet': 'The popular tourist destination is now in the top 20 U.S. states and territories for cases per capita, according to a New York Times database.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As coronavirus cases and hospitalizations rise across the country, some areas with low vaccination rates have been hit hard, like Louisiana, Florida and Mississippi.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/11/world/11virus-briefing-virgin-islands1/merlin_183585192_48f62913-bf1a-40c6-b132-2e71eaf01423-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/11/world/11virus-briefing-virgin-islands1/merlin_183585192_48f62913-bf1