rs and military had been given every chance to determine their future, he said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Biden offered a defiant defense on Monday of his decision to withdraw troops from Afghanistan, blaming the swift collapse of the Afghan government and chaotic scenes at the Kabul airport on the refusal of the country’s military to stand and fight in the face of the Taliban advance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden stands behind Afghan withdrawal, despite ‘hard and messy’ final days.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facing Afghan Chaos, Biden Defends Exit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Afghan National Security Forces', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kabul International Airport', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-16T14:34:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear and David E. Sanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c723c347-2d45-5f7c-b7a6-89ec6fb16378', 'word_count': 1510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c723c347-2d45-5f7c-b7a6-89ec6fb16378'}, {'abstract': 'Use Atlantic bonito for a Northeastern spin on the Hawaiian classic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/16/dining/fishing-for-tuna-poke.html', 'snippet': 'Use Atlantic bonito for a Northeastern spin on the Hawaiian classic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. The shorebirds that passed me on their way north after the winter are starting to push south along the coast of New England and New York, which means the fall run is starting and not just for birds. We’ll see striped bass heading south pretty soon as well, along with false albacore and bluefish. If we’re lucky — if I’m lucky, out on a boat somewhere where there’s current and bait — there’ll be Atlantic bonito at some point, too, feeding on spearing and, hopefully, one of my badly tied flies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/14/magazine/14mag-eat-image1-copy/14mag-eat-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/14/magazine/14mag-eat-image1-copy/14mag-eat-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/14/magazine/14mag-eat-image1-copy/14mag-eat-image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption':