, sells foods made in the Empire State online, and it ships nationwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taste NY, created by the New York State Department of Agriculture and Markets and the governor’s office in 2013 to promote locally made food products, has made the foods and other local items available online. The digital marketplace is run by the Cornell Cooperative Extension of Sullivan County. The products, like pickles, jams, condiments, sauces, syrups and the like, are sorted by region. They’re the same products that are sold at many official state stores throughout New York.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/18/dining/18BurnerState/16BurnerState-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/18/dining/18BurnerState/16BurnerState-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/18/dining/18BurnerState/16BurnerState-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/18/dining/18BurnerState/16BurnerState-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/18/dining/18BurnerState/16BurnerState-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/18/dining/18BurnerState/16BurnerState-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 