name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Bridge (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Bridge Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chinatown (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Domino Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dumbo (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Tryon Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'High Line (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Red Hook (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-18T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Carmel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carmel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5f07c88-71d0-5e4a-bbdb-9d76f6ab814d', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5f07c88-71d0-5e4a-bbdb-9d76f6ab814d'}, {'abstract': 'Drying zucchini outdoors is ideal, but this agrodolce can be made even without a Mediterranean balcony.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/18/magazine/zucchini-agrodulce-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'Drying zucchini outdoors is ideal, but this agrodolce can be made even without a Mediterranean balcony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first place I saw the sun used as an oven was Greece, on a trip with my mom. When we came back from lunch to our rented whitewashed cool room in someone’s whitewashed cool house on a small whitewashed island — the woman of that house had picked her ripe, jammy figs in the morning and was laying them out on the roof. There they dried in the sun all afternoon, while her husband sat in the shade of the fig trees and mended his fishing nets after the morning’s haul. I’ve since seen people use the sun to dry grapes, fish, mushrooms, herbs, shrimp and lavender. Wherever there is a cobalt blue window frame, there is surely a bushy wreath of vibrant red chiles nailed to it. My mother-in-law Alda, who has since died, used to set large round platters of her tomato purée out on the splintering wicker furniture on her terrace in Santa Maria di Leuca in the south of Italy and let it bake all afternoon under the intense Pugliese sun, from ragù red at noon to dark, leathery ruby by sundown.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/22/magazine/22mag-eat/22mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/22/magazine/22mag-eat/22mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/22/magazine/22mag-eat/22mag-eat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/22/magazine/22mag-eat/22mag-eat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1542, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/22/magazine/22mag-eat/22mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/22/magazine/22mag-eat/22mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/22/magazine/22mag-eat/22mag-eat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooking Without an Oven, the Southern Italian Way', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Place in the Sun: Drying zucchini outdoors is ideal, but this agrodolce can be made even without a Mediterranean balcony. ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zucchini', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ovens and Stoves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olive Oil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-18T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabrielle Hamilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabrielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02cc7fc6-2355-525e-b7a6-6b07c02bc3dc', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02cc7fc6-2355-525e-b7a6-6b07c02bc3dc'}, {'abstract': 'Talking to children about various types of protest can empower them to make their voices heard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/18/parenting/protests-racism-kids.html', 'snippet': 'Talking to children about various types of protest can empower them to make their voices heard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The spring and early summer of 2020 was a tough time for me and many other parents. The deaths of George Floyd, Breonna Taylor and the spotlight on previous victims such as Elijah McClain broke our hearts again and again as we watched graphic videos of police-involved killings and stayed glued to the news. There were days that I woke up crying and went to bed crying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/17/well/PAR-NL-PROTEST3/merlin_174537078_ec1d900e-1a16-4d92-bcbb-7addd8fb3702-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/17/well/PAR-NL-PROTEST3/merlin_174537078_ec1d900e-1a16-4d92-bcbb-7addd8fb3702-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/17/well/PAR-NL-PROTEST3/merlin_174537078_ec1d900e-1a16-4d92-bcbb-7addd8fb3702-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/17/well/PAR-NL-PROTEST3/merlin_174537078_ec1d900e-1a16-4d92-bcbb-7addd8fb3702-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1637, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/17/well/PAR-NL-PROTEST3/PAR-NL-PROTEST3-thumbSta