lide, you can see forever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/18/sports/parenting-safety-freedom.html', 'snippet': 'From the top of the big kids’ slide, you can see forever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rafa wants to go on the big kids’ slide. He has taken a few trips down the smaller one and enjoyed them enough, but at 2½ he already seems to understand that the greater the risk, the greater the thrill. He walks with the confidence of a matador toward the long, green plastic chute, which rises 12 feet into the air, a steep, curving structure that sits near a sign saying it was designed for children between the ages of 5 and 12.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/sports/00freedom-grandson-toned/00freedom-grandson-toned-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/13/sports/00freedom-grandson-toned/00freedom-grandson-toned-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/sports/00freedom-grandson-toned/00freedom-grandson-toned-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/sports/00freedom-grandson-toned/00freedom-grandson-toned-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/sports/00freedom-grandson-toned/00freedom-grandson-toned-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/13/sports/00freedom-grandson-toned/00freedom-grandson-toned-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/13/sports/00freedom-grandson-toned/00freedom-grandson-toned-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Thrill Seeker', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Thrill Seeker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playgrounds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-18T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd42bb4a-5297-53fd-88b6-3206c7e17b92', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd42bb4a-5297-53fd-88b6-3206c7e17b92'}, {'abstract': 'Are students being taught that the United States is racist? Should they be?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/18/opinion/critical-race-theory-us-schools.html', 'snippet': 'Are students being taught that the United States is racist? Should they be?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many politicians and parents, there’s growing concern over critical race theory. It maintains that race and racism in America are about not individual actors and actions as much as bigger structures that lead to and maintain gaps between racial groups. The theory started in the legal academy, and some fear that it has begun to take over the American education system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': '