sent their community.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/19/nyregion/chinatown-museum-protests.html', 'snippet': 'In Manhattan’s Chinatown, anti-gentrification protesters are furious over funding granted to a museum that they say doesn’t represent their community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twice a week, Li Zhen Tan, a former dim sum server, plants herself in front of the Museum of Chinese in America in Chinatown and joins the fervent chants of dozens of others like her who have congregated there.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/07/28/nyregion/00nychinatown1/00nychinatown1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/07/28/nyregion/00nychinatown1/00nychinatown1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/07/28/nyregion/00nychinatown1/00nychinatown1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/07/28/nyregion/00nychinatown1/00nychinatown1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/07/28/nyregion/00nychinatown1/00nychinatown1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/07/28/nyregion/00nychinatown1/00nychinatown1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/07/28/nyregion/00nychinatown1/00nychinatown1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Some People in Chinatown Oppose a Museum Dedicated to Their Culture', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Chinatown, Protesters Jab Museum Over Funds  To Preserve Asian Culture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gentrification', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jing Fong (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Chinese in America', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maasbach, Nancy Yao', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chinatown (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-19T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kimiko de Freytas-Tamura', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kimiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Freytas-Tamura', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93a0fdac-bc00-5568-ac19-b79aa995e0f6', 'word_count': 1568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93a0fdac-bc00-5568-ac19-b79aa995e0f6'}, {'abstract': 'Our data is as secure as their policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/19/opinion/apple-iphone-privacy.html', 'snippet': 'Our data is as secure as their policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even iPhone users with nothing to hide could be forgiven for being a little creeped out that Apple will scan their photos and see if they match existing databases of known illegal pornographic images. Privacy experts called the idea a potential back door for governments to request or demand scans for other images or files. Some of Apple’s own employees are reportedly pushing back on the idea.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/20bensinger-inyt/19bensinger-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/20bensinger-inyt/19bensinger-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 853}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/20bensinger-inyt/19bensinger-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 721, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/20bensinger-inyt/19bensinger-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1442, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/20bensinger-inyt/19bensinger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/20bensinger-inyt/19bensinger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/opinion/20bensinger-inyt/19bensinger-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple’s Illusion of Privacy Is Getting Harder to Sell', 'kicker': 'Greg Bensinger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Privacy’s Illusion Is Getting Harder to Sell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-19T09:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bensinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bensinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/00545841-4940-591c-85d3-4d3c35447866', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00545841-4940-591c-85d3-4d3c35447866'}, {'abstract': 'For Afghans, the war isn’t over simply because the United States declared it so. The nightmare doesn’t end after the last American leaves. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/19/opinion/afghanistan-vietnam-war-refugees.html', 'snippet': 'For Afghans, the war isn’t over simply because the United States declared it so. The nightmare doesn’t end after the last American leaves. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was 4 years old when Saigon fell, so I do not remember any of it. I count myself lucky, since many Vietnamese who survived the end of that war were greatly traumatized by it. The collapse of the American-backed Southern regime began in my Central Highlands hometown, Ban Me Thuot, in March 1975. In less than two months, all of South Vietnam capitulated to the North Vietnamese. Soldiers fled in chaotic retreat among civilians. My mother, brother and I were among them. We left behind my adopted sister. After walking nearly 200 kilometers to escape the advancing North Vietnamese army, the three of us made it to the seaside city of Nha Trang, where we managed to find a boat to take us to Saigon where my father was.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/21/opinion/21Nguyen2-inyt/17Nguyen2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/21/opinion/21Nguyen2-inyt/17Nguyen2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/21/opinion/21Nguyen2-inyt/17Nguyen2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/21/opinion/21Nguyen2-inyt/17Nguyen2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/21/opinion/21Nguyen2-inyt/17Nguyen2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/21/opinion/21Nguyen2-inyt/17Nguyen2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/21/opinion/21Nguyen2-inyt/17Nguyen2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150