 by some wealthy nations to start administering coronavirus booster shots, saying the decisions “make a mockery of vaccine equity” when the African continent is still struggling to get vaccine supplies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Booster shots ‘make a mockery of vaccine equity,’ the W.H.O.’s Africa director says.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Africa Official Says Boosters Cheat Others', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Delta Variant', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disease Rates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moeti, Matshidiso', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-19T14:57:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abdi Latif Dahir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abdi', 'middlename': 'Latif', 'lastname': 'Dahir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a15eee2-45c7-5881-af7f-575c281bf9d2', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a15eee2-45c7-5881-af7f-575c281bf9d2'}, {'abstract': 'In his latest, the director Neill Blomkamp plays around with different genre elements but never figures out how to make them cohere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/19/movies/demonic-review.html', 'snippet': 'In his latest, the director Neill Blomkamp plays around with different genre elements but never figures out how to make them cohere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Flat acting, risible dialogue, a witless story — sometimes when a movie hits this trifecta so completely, it engenders a feeling of disreputable pleasure. It’s bad, and you know it, and maybe the filmmakers know it too. How could they not? Yet somehow all the suboptimal (inept, incoherent) elements mysteriously cohere into a work that finds its own perverse groove. “Demonic” is not such a singular amusement. It’s just a drag.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/19/arts/19demonic-review/19demonic-review-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/19/arts/19demonic-review/19demonic-review-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/19/arts/19demonic-review/19demonic-review-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/19/arts/19demonic-review/19demonic-review-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1620, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/19/arts/19demonic-review/19demonic-review-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/19/arts/19demonic-review/19demonic-review-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarg