ural disasters, the impact of climate change on American life is now more palpable than ever. More than 60 percent of Americans say it has already affected their communities, according to the Pew Research Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/us/climate-grief-callout/climate-grief-callout-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/12/us/climate-grief-callout/climate-grief-callout-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/us/climate-grief-callout/climate-grief-callout-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/us/climate-grief-callout/climate-grief-callout-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/us/climate-grief-callout/climate-grief-callout-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/12/us/climate-grief-callout/climate-grief-callout-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/12/us/climate-grief-callout/climate-grief-callout-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Has Climate Change Upended Your Life? We Want to Hear from You.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotion)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'internal-open-access', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-20T12:05:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/840a0e51-9024-5724-90eb-4d771ab46ae4', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/840a0e51-9024-5724-90eb-4d771ab46ae4'}, {'abstract': 'The investor’s response to a lawsuit marks another twist in his efforts to save his billion-dollar blank-check vehicle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/20/business/dealbook/bill-ackman-spac-sparc.html', 'snippet': 'The investor’s response to a lawsuit marks another twist in his efforts to save his billion-dollar blank-check vehicle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Ackman, the billionaire hedge fund manager, is pivoting again to try to save Pershing Square Tontine Holdings, his $4 billion special purpose acquisition company, which has faced a series of setbacks since it launched a year ago. In a letter to investors posted late last night, he proposed a radical rethink that could lead to the SPAC shutting down, returning its cash to investors and being reborn in a new guise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/business/20db-newsletter-ackman/merlin_191045535_1d0703cf-a613-4e49-b18c-ef05671a9b1d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge',