'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Orr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4913a87-6b99-5cb1-ba5c-6185e6da35bc', 'word_count': 1242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4913a87-6b99-5cb1-ba5c-6185e6da35bc'}, {'abstract': 'An update on Van Cleef & Arpels’s Jarretière design, this gem-encrusted bracelet from the brand mimics the sky at dawn and dusk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/20/t-magazine/van-cleef-arche-solaire-bracelet.html', 'snippet': 'An update on Van Cleef & Arpels’s Jarretière design, this gem-encrusted bracelet from the brand mimics the sky at dawn and dusk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alfred Van Cleef, the son of a diamond cutter, married Estelle Arpels, the daughter of a precious stones dealer and, about a decade later, in 1906, the house of Van Cleef & Arpels opened its doors on Paris’s Place Vendôme. By the 1920s, the maison was experimenting with exotic Art Deco creations and, in the early ’30s, it pioneered a groundbreaking new technique called the Mystery Set, by which gemstones could be arranged in a mosaiclike pattern without any visible supports. Its sautoirs, minaudières and brooches quickly became favorites among royals and Hollywood stars including Marlene Dietrich, for whom Van Cleef created one of its most iconic designs, the Jarretière bracelet, in 1937. The story goes that Dietrich gave a handful of her gemstone-studded pieces to Louis Arpels, the brother of Estelle and one of the company’s founders, and asked him to create something special. And so the Jarretière was born: The modernist platinum cuff featured an exaggerated, asymmetrical loop covered in cushion-cut rubies set atop twin bucklelike bands of baguette-and-pavé-set white diamonds. (The piece’s name translates to “garter,” and indeed the design resembles the band worn around the top of a woman’s stocking.) Dietrich famously wore it in Alfred Hitchcock’s 1950 noir thriller, “Stage Fright” (she also insisted on head-to-toe Dior for the role), and to the Academy Awards a year later.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '139', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/t-magazine/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/20/t-magazine/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/t-magazine/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/t-magazine/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/t-magazine/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/20/t-magazine/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/t-magazine/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy/20tmag-vancleef-slide-YTPI-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Celestial Cuff Modeled After One Made for Marlene Dietrich', 'kicker': 'First of its kind, last of its kind', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Van Cleef & Arpels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dietrich, Marlene', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bos, Nicolas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-20T13:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Talbot', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Talbot', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6acda836-40de-5ab0-87dd-74c73b2d033f', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6acda836-40de-5ab0-87dd-74c73b2d033f'}, {'abstract': 'A version of “A Midsummer Night’s Dream” is planned, along with the company’s puppet series, an examination of the Tulsa Race Massacre and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/20/theater/lamama-season.html', 'snippet': 'A version of “A Midsummer Night’s Dream” is planned, along with the company’s puppet series, an examination of the Tulsa Race Massacre and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a season that is expected to include the reopening of its flagship theater after a three-year, $24 million renovation, La MaMa Experimental Theater Club will present an Indigenous take on “A Midsummer Night’s Dream,” a theatrical examination of the Tulsa Race Massacre and a vaudeville concert that explores the history of cannabis.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subt