 campaign of terror and arbitrary arrests, thousands of activists are working clandestinely to spread dissent and undermine the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/20/world/europe/belarus-opposition-protests.html', 'snippet': 'Despite a government campaign of terror and arbitrary arrests, thousands of activists are working clandestinely to spread dissent and undermine the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GRODNO, Belarus — The streets of Belarus are quiet now, a year after President Aleksandr G. Lukashenko brutally crushed a wave of mass protests; billboards and tidy landscaping proclaiming 2021 the “Year of National Unity” are ubiquitous.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/world/20belarus1/merlin_193345704_aeec3de9-86f6-413c-aa69-04807e52b4d5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/20/world/20belarus1/merlin_193345704_aeec3de9-86f6-413c-aa69-04807e52b4d5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/world/20belarus1/merlin_193345704_aeec3de9-86f6-413c-aa69-04807e52b4d5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/world/20belarus1/merlin_193345704_aeec3de9-86f6-413c-aa69-04807e52b4d5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/world/20belarus1/20belarus1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'c