 Islamic State might launch an attack to damage the Taliban’s sense of control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Panic and desperation rose Saturday among thousands of Afghans struggling to flee the week-old Taliban takeover of Afghanistan, as gates to the Kabul airport were closed off and the U.S. embassy warned American citizens to stay away from the airport, citing “potential security threats outside the gates.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fears Rise About Safety of Afghan Airport as U.S. Warns Americans to Stay Away', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Embassy Warns Americans to Avoid Kabul Airport Amid Threats', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFGHAN-AMERICANS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kabul International Airport', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baradar, Abdul Ghani', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-21T15:49:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Zucchino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zucchino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccd79adc-5410-5b94-9509-82e8031b774d', 'word_count': 1844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccd79adc-5410-5b94-9509-82e8031b774d'}, {'abstract': 'Take a road trip through America with this John Suarez invention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/21/crosswords/variety-reinstatements.html', 'snippet': 'Take a road trip through America with this John Suarez invention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'REINSTATEMENTS — Every August we get an out-of-the-ordinary variety puzzle from the National Puzzlers’ League Convention, which most recently took place in Washington, D.C., last month. This is the 181st Convention, impressively enough (they don’t go back to 1840, but the League formed in 1883 and the conventions have been held for a very long time). The program is similarly imposing, stuffed with quizzes and contests, including the word-pairing challenge we have today. I think this is a fun one, not too esoteric, although I wouldn’t want to have to speed-solve it competitively because a few stumpers had me mulling for quite a bit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Reinstatements', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-08-21T16:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af1b317e-0e66-53f4-84ee-2b800fb419f8', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af1b317e-0e66-53f4-84ee-2b800fb419f8'}, {'abstract': 'President Biden promised an orderly withdrawal. That pledge, compounded by missed signals and miscalculations, proved impossible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/21/us/politics/biden-taliban-afghanistan-kabul.html', 'snippet': 'President Biden promised an orderly withdrawal. That pledge, compounded by missed signals and miscalculations, proved impossible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The nation’s top national security officials assembled at the Pentagon early on April 24 for a secret meeting to plan the final withdrawal of American troops from Afghanistan. It was two weeks after President Biden had announced the exit over the objection of his generals, but now they were carrying out his orders.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Miscue After Miscue, U.S. Exit Plan Unravels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Miscue After Miscue, Exit Plan Unravels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blinken, Antony J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghani, Ashraf', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Afghan National Security Forces', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-21T16:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear, David E. Sanger, Helene Cooper, Eric Schmitt, Julian E. Barnes and Lara Jakes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f751ec06-b6a5-5db9-8a58-315be1885eed', 'word_count': 2814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f751ec06-b6a5-5db9-8a58-315be1885eed'}, {'abstract': 'Some Americans made it through the chaos at the airport despite warnings by the U.S. State Department to wait for orders to evacuate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/21/world/asia/kabul-airport-afghanistan-security.html', 'snippet': 'Some Americans made it through the chaos at the airport despite warnings by the U.S. State Department to wait for orders to evacuate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The State Department and Pentagon on Saturday gave conflicting messages to Americans seeking to flee Afghanistan through Hamid Karzai International Airport in Kabul, as security conditions continued to deteriorate at the remaining gateway out of the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The situation at Kabul’s airport deteriorates as diplomats warn of threats.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-21T16:43:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/238da01f-8f1e-58d9-babd-3ed7ec8be41e', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/238da01f-8f1e-58d9-babd-3ed7ec8be41e'}, {'abstract': 'She gave them a sense of identity and culture and helped legitimize American Sign Language, which she considered her native language.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/21/us/barbara-kannapell-dead.html', 'snippet': 'She gave them a sense of identity and culture and helped legitimize American Sign Language, which she considered her native language.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barbara Kannapell, a world-renowned deaf activist who made it her life’s work to empower deaf and hard-of-hearing people with a sense of identity and an appreciation for their own distinct culture, and who advanced the idea that American Sign Language was a legitimate, foundational language, died on Aug. 11 in Washington. She was 83. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/26/obituaries/Kannapell-01/merlin_193366266_6fdee6cc-4dc0-4598-84fa-3510005ece38-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 892, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/26/obituaries/Kannapell-01/merlin_193366266_6fdee6cc-4dc0-4598-84fa-3510005ece38-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 892}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/26/obituaries/Kannapell-01/merlin