, 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/dining/23burner-melon2/23burner-melon2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/25/dining/23burner-melon2/23burner-melon2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/dining/23burner-melon2/23burner-melon2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/dining/23burner-melon2/23burner-melon2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/dining/23burner-melon2/23burner-melon2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/25/dining/23burner-melon2/23burner-melon2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/dining/23burner-melon2/23burner-melon2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disappointing Melon? Try These Tricks.', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Rescue: Mediocre Melon?  Try These Tricks.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Melons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-23T23:50:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1107c67-db99-5418-8d95-9ada162cb7bf', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1107c67-db99-5418-8d95-9ada162cb7bf'}, {'abstract': 'The author will discuss Rosh Hashana and suggest recipes during a virtual event hosted by a new food-focused cultural center in Tel Aviv.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/23/dining/asif-culinary-institute-of-israel.html', 'snippet': 'The author will discuss Rosh Hashana and suggest recipes during a virtual event hosted by a new food-focused cultural center in Tel Aviv.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Asif: Culinary Institute of Israel, a new food-focused cultural center with a library, test kitchen, rooftop farm, gallery and cafe, opened last month in Tel Aviv. It’s the work of Naama Shefi, who created and runs the nonprofit Jewish Food Society in the United States to foster Jewish food culture, and Terry Kassel, chairwoman of the board of Start-Up Nation Central, an Israeli nonprofit promoting innovation. For one of its first programs, the cookbook author Adeena Sussman will discuss food for the Rosh Hashana holiday and suggest recipes from cookbooks she wants to see in Asif’s library.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/dining/23burner-Asif/merlin_193452276_858d4b17-55e7-47f3-9cf7-54da7a3046e5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/25/dining/23burner-Asif/merlin_193452276_858d4b17-55e7-47f3-9cf7-54da7a3046e5-articleLarge.