ype_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/35033f27-caad-523b-952c-0f74c33b73e2', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35033f27-caad-523b-952c-0f74c33b73e2'}, {'abstract': 'The point of winning is to use your power well. Then you might actually get to keep it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/24/opinion/democrats-bipartisan-infrastructure-bill.html', 'snippet': 'The point of winning is to use your power well. Then you might actually get to keep it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Popular or unpopular, good economy or bad, the president’s party almost always loses seats in midterm elections. That there are so few exceptions — Franklin Roosevelt and the Democrats in 1934, Bill Clinton and the Democrats in 1998, and George W. Bush and the Republicans in 2002 — proves the rule.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/opinion/24bouie-lead/merlin_190175880_11593bfe-fc1d-42a7-8dc6-2c68fe402399-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/25/opinion/24bouie-lead/merlin_190175880_11593bfe-fc1d-42a7-8dc6-2c68fe402399-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/opinion/24bouie-lead/merlin_190175880_11593bfe-fc1d-42a7-8dc6-2c68fe402399-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/opinion/24bouie-lead/merlin_190175880_11593bfe-fc1d-42a7-8dc6-2c68fe402399-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/opinion/24bouie-lead/merlin_190175880_11593bfe-fc1d-42a7-8dc6-2c68fe402399-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/25/opinion/24bouie-lead/merlin_190175880_11593bfe-fc1d-42a7-8dc6-2c68fe402399-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/opinion/24bouie-lead/merlin_190175880_11593bfe-fc1d-42a7-8dc6-2c68fe402399-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The 9 Democrats Making Nancy Pelosi’s Life Harder Are Making a Big Mistake', 'kicker': 'Jamelle Bouie', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Jobs Plan (2021)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-24T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jamelle Bouie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jamelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bouie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b00ca037-ad06-5d66-a8ac-e71079ae76c1', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b00ca037-ad06-5d66-a8ac-e71079ae76c1'}, {'abstract': 'Research suggests that people with freely moving thoughts are happier. Easy, repetitive activities like walking can help get you in the right mindset.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/24/magazine/how-to-let-your-mind-wander.html', 'snippet': 'Research suggests that people with freely moving thoughts are happier. Easy, repetitive activities like walking can help get you in the right mindset.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Sometimes you just want to let your mind go free,” says Julia Kam, a cognitive neuroscientist who directs the Internal Attention Lab at the University of Calgary. Kam became interested in her subject 15 years ago as an undergraduate struggling with her own distracted thoughts during lectures. “I came into the field wanting to find a cure,” she says. But the deeper she got into research, the more she came to appreciate the freedom of an unfocused mind. “When your thoughts are just jumping from one topic to the next without an overarching theme or goal, that can be very liberating,” she says.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/29/magazine/29mag-tip/29mag-tip-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/29/magazine/29mag-tip/29mag-tip-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/29/magazine/29mag-tip/29mag-tip-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/29/magazine/29mag-tip/29mag-tip-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048,