lue': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Airbnb', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chesky, Brian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-24T11:04:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eshe Nelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eshe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b3e21a1-5126-5b62-a257-9dea6f1f1447', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b3e21a1-5126-5b62-a257-9dea6f1f1447'}, {'abstract': 'The Imperial Family’s support goes back to the 1964 Paralympics, which were held in Tokyo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/24/sports/emperor-naruhito-paralympics-japan.html', 'snippet': 'The Imperial Family’s support goes back to the 1964 Paralympics, which were held in Tokyo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — His Majesty the Emperor of Japan, Naruhito, will officially declare the Paralympic Games open. Japan’s Imperial family has a long history of support for the Paralympics: The current emperor’s parents, Emperor Emeritus Akihito and Empress Emerita Michiko, adopted the 1964 Paralympics in Tokyo as one of their primary causes when they were Crown Prince and Princess. Tokyo is the first city to host the Paralympics twice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/24/sports/24paralympic-briefing-imperial1/merlin_193617702_5c39bea2-e747-4c65-9c21-2400b57dc56d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/24/sports/24paralympic-briefing-imperial1/merlin_193617702_5c39bea2-