 'This verbatim hockey drama considers issues of masculinity and the peculiar ownership that fans feel toward a team and its players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2017 season didn’t start too badly. The New York Islanders, a National Hockey League team with a new coach and a newish berth at the Barclays Center in Brooklyn, might have allowed a few too many shots on goal, but they still won most of their games. A couple of months later, in December, it all began to go wrong. Then it went more wrong. The defense fell apart. The team missed the playoffs. John Tavares, the Islanders’ captain and star player, departed for the Toronto Maple Leafs. Fans revolted.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/24/arts/24islander-1/merlin_193558731_26f05a22-37c9-4746-9d35-aebc2b9aa2f4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/24/arts/24islander-1/merlin_193558731_26f05a22-37c9-4746-9d35-aebc2b9aa2f4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/24/arts/24islander-1/merlin_193558731_26f05a22-37c9-4746-9d35-aebc2b9aa2f4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/24/arts/24islander-1/merlin_193558731_26f05a22-37c9-4746-9d35-aebc2b9aa2f4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1494, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/24/arts/24islander-1/24islander-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'cr