 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lorde Opts Out on the Provocatively Subdued ‘Solar Power’', 'kicker': 'Album Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Ease  In the Sun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lorde', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Solar Power (Album)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Antonoff, Jack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-25T17:49:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Zoladz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zoladz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/481c8732-cdcb-56cb-aef4-e7772bca168a', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/481c8732-cdcb-56cb-aef4-e7772bca168a'}, {'abstract': 'Matthias Kaiser’s extensive travels, and apprenticeships in Japan, continue to inform his nuanced, stylistically wide-ranging vessels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/25/t-magazine/matthias-kaiser-ceramics-art.html', 'snippet': 'Matthias Kaiser’s extensive travels, and apprenticeships in Japan, continue to inform his nuanced, stylistically wide-ranging vessels.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I was an incredibly naughty teenager,” says the ceramist Matthias Kaiser, who grew up in the Austrian city of Graz. “One day I just disappeared.” In 1989, at age 19, he sold his car and bought a one-way plane ticket to New York in the hopes of becoming a jazz musician (he played the soprano saxophone) — only for a chance encounter to radically alter his plan. Walking along West Broadway about a year after he arrived, he came across a stall where a group of potters were selling traditional, handcrafted Pennsylvanian ceramics and, though simple, the blue-and-white spongeware vessels captivated him. “I just couldn’t believe they were selling these objects that they had made themselves,” he says. “It blew me away.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/t-magazine/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/25/t-magazine/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/t-magazine/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/t-magazine/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/t-magazine/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/25/t-magazine/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F/24tmag-matthiaskaiser-slide-6T9F-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/t-magazine/2