': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/2251b078-fd3c-5e5f-b168-5ed62108aa0e'}, {'abstract': 'Congress needs to stop abdicating its constitutional duty to determine whether, where and whom America should fight.\xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/25/opinion/declaration-war-president-Congress.html', 'snippet': 'Congress needs to stop abdicating its constitutional duty to determine whether, where and whom America should fight.\xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suppose President Biden came before Congress to announce that ending the war in Afghanistan was only the beginning. In recent years, the United States has used force on the ground or conducted strikes from the air in at least nine countries: not only Afghanistan, but also Iraq, Kenya, Libya, Mali, Pakistan, Somalia, Syria and Yemen. These wars go on in part because one person wages them. Congress has abdicated its constitutional duty to determine whether, where and whom America should fight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/27/opinion/25Wertheim/25Wertheim-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/27/opinion/25Wertheim/25Wertheim-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/27/opinion/25Wertheim/25Wertheim-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/27/opinion/25Wertheim/25Wertheim-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/27/opinion/25Werthei