assing San Francisco. At the same time, tens of thousands of people are millions of dollars behind on rent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On her first day in office this week, Gov. Kathy Hochul said that she would move to strengthen New York’s beleaguered effort to distribute pandemic rent relief, highlighting the plight of hundreds of thousands of struggling New Yorkers who are at risk of being evicted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/nyregion/25nyrent01/merlin_193437774_8987dfc2-85d5-4dbe-b08c-5eded4c6eec4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/25/nyregion/25nyrent01/merlin_193437774_8987dfc2-85d5-4dbe-b08c-5eded4c6eec4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/nyregion/25nyrent01/merlin_193437774_8987dfc2-85d5-4dbe-b08c-5eded4c6eec4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/nyregion/25nyrent01/merlin_193437774_8987dfc2-85d5-4dbe-b08c-5eded4c6eec4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/nyregion/25nyrent01/25nyrent01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/25/nyregion/25nyrent01/25nyrent01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/25/nyregion/25nyrent01/25nyrent01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York City Rents Rise, Even as Thousands Struggle to Pay', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Site Finds New York Rents Surged to Nation’s Highest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hochul, Kathleen C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-25T22:50:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mihir Zaveri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mihir', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zaveri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f99ae1d-c0eb-50ab-a3a0-88e71f6599a0', 'word_count': 1200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f99ae1d-c0eb-50ab-a3a0-88e71f6599a0'}, {'abstract': 'Mount Vernon is one of scores of cities around the country with an outdated or overtaxed sewage system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/25/opinion/environmental-racism-wastewater-broken.html', 'snippet': 'Mount Vernon is one of scores of cities around the country with an outdated or overtaxed sewage system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Linda McNeil had barely settled into her newly built home a 20-minute drive from Manhattan when raw sewage first flooded her basement. That was 21 years ago, and the problem has only grown worse. Like others among the predominantly Black population in the city of Mount Vernon, N.Y.,