ism Causes a Hygienic Hell', 'kicker': 'guest essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Racism That Spews Into Your Sink', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sewers and Sewage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mount Vernon (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-25T23:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Flowers and Mitchell Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flowers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mitchell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ea6d899-12be-58a4-9dc8-ee2ba77659ae', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ea6d899-12be-58a4-9dc8-ee2ba77659ae'}, {'abstract': 'No proof of vaccination or a recent negative coronavirus test will be required for fans to enter the grounds, and no masks will be required when they are outdoors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/25/sports/tennis/us-open-fans-covid-masks.html', 'snippet': 'No proof of vaccination or a recent negative coronavirus test will be required for fans to enter the grounds, and no masks will be required when they are outdoors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The U.S. Open welcomed almost 750,000 fans onto its grounds in 2019 during its two-week run, and comparable numbers