rl': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/26/opinion/sway-kara-swisher-randi-weingarten.html', 'snippet': 'The most powerful teachers’ union president in America discusses school reopening, mask mandates and vaccine-or-test requirements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the pandemic has pushed the country into a debate about when and how to reopen schools, Randi Weingarten has faced the ire of parents, teachers, school boards and — of course — Fox News. Weingarten, the president of the American Federation of Teachers, leads a union of 1.7 million educators across the nation. She’s been on the hook for pressing to keep schools closed last fall and supporting mask mandates in classrooms this year. And most recently, she drew criticism from her members when she personally endorsed a vaccine mandate and promised to work with states and school boards that are seeking to enact vaccine mandates or vaccinate-or-test requirements for teachers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/26/opinion/26sway--weingarten-image/26sway--weingarten-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/26/opinion/26sway--weingarten-image/26sway--weingarten-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/26/opinion/26sway--weingarten-image/26sway--weingarten-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/26/opinion/26sway--weingarten-image/26sway--weingarten-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/26/opinion/26sway--weingarten-image/26sway--weingarten-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/26/opinion/26sway--weingarten-image/26sway--weingarten-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/26/opinion/26sway--weingarten-image/26sway--weingarten-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Vaccine Mandates for Teachers Have Been a Harder Sell Than Mask Mandates for Kids', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weingarten, Randi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF TEACHERS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Reopenings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Masks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-26T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By ‘Sway'", 'person': [{'firstname': "Sway'", 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e9edfed-6e3e-5b8d-92b9-2a96ee901c11', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e9edfed-6e3e-5b8d-92b9-2a96ee901c11'}, {'abstract': 'Our ignominious exit reflects the failure of America’s foreign policy establishment at both prediction and policymaking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/26/opinion/afghanistan-us-withdrawal.html', 'snippet': 'Our ignominious exit reflects the failure of America’s foreign policy establishment at both prediction and policymaking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2005, two of my colleagues at The American Prospect, Sam Rosenfeld and Matt Yglesias, wrote an essay I think about often. It was called “The Incompetence Dodge,” and it argued that American policymakers and pundits routinely try to rescue the reputation of bad ideas by attributing their failure to poor execution. At the time, they were writing about the liberal hawks who were blaming the catastrophe of the Iraq war on the Bush administration’s maladministration rather than rethinking the enterprise in its totality. But the same dynamic suffuses the recriminations over the Afghanistan withdrawal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/28/opinion/26klein-lead/26klein-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/28/opinion/26klein-lead/26klein-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/28/opinion/26klein-lead/26klein-lead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/28/opinion/26kl