yt://article/3b94d405-8fd7-5af4-9aad-103116fe2a46'}, {'abstract': 'As flames approached her family’s hometown in California, a reporter who normally works in New York knew she could lend a hand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/26/insider/dixie-fire-taylorsville.html', 'snippet': 'As flames approached her family’s hometown in California, a reporter who normally works in New York knew she could lend a hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Annie Correal reports on immigrant communities for The Times’s Metro desk. But lately, her byline has appeared above coverage of the Dixie fire in Northern California, currently the largest wildfire in the country. Ms. Correal has close family ties to the Indian Valley, a ranching area in the Sierra Nevada threatened by the flames. A week ago, she boarded a plane to lend her local expertise to the National desk. In a recent article, she tells a personal story about a group of people defending their homes. Ms. Correal reflected on the assignment in an interview. Her edited responses are below.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/26/us/26insider-dixie-1/merlin_193436310_d6d21b78-8153-4660-bc49-3f2c822478b8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/26/us/26insider-dixie-1/merlin_193436310_d6d21b78-8153-4660-bc49-3f2c822478b8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/26/us/26insider-dixie-1/merlin_193436310_d6d21b78-8153-4660-bc49-3f2c822478b8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/26/us/26insider