tion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/806c294c-7a92-5d7b-9cba-0ae74a6c8ac4', 'word_count': 1612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/806c294c-7a92-5d7b-9cba-0ae74a6c8ac4'}, {'abstract': 'Try these three methods to capture the essence of summer fruit in jams and jellies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/30/dining/preserves-jams-jellies.html', 'snippet': 'Try these three methods to capture the essence of summer fruit in jams and jellies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s almost no way around the fact that making preserves is a process. But for me that’s what is so enjoyable about it. I am, to a fault, a process person. I revel in precision and attention to detail — these are my superpowers. They’re why I’m drawn to making preserves. In returning to the tradition each year, I have found that I’m always seeking the same thing: to capture memories of farm visits, perfect produce and the season’s warmth in small glass jars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/dining/30Preserves1/merlin_193667565_201ea613-e2c4-41c2-97ef-3b6bfe4d597c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/01/dining/30Preserves1/merlin_193667565_201ea613-e2c4-41c2-97ef-3b6bfe4d597c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/dining/30Preserves1/merlin_193667565_201ea613-e2c4-41c2-97ef-3b6bfe4d597c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/dining/30Preserves1/merlin_193667565_201ea613-e2c4-41c2-97ef-3b6bfe4d597c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width':