 Raisa Gorbachev, and portrays the former leader in all his humanity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/30/theater/gorbachev-play-moscow.html', 'snippet': 'The Latvian director Alvis Hermanis’s bioplay is an ode to the love story of Mikhail and Raisa Gorbachev, and portrays the former leader in all his humanity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — In August 1991, Mikhail Gorbachev, the last leader of the Soviet Union, returned to Moscow with his family from house arrest in Crimea after a K.G.B.-managed anti-democracy coup had failed to depose him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/arts/30gorbachev-notebook-1/merlin_186188976_972459c5-3ee0-430e-ae05-3a16f96ab72a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/01/arts/30gorbachev-notebook-1/merlin_186188976_972459c5-3ee0-430e-ae05-3a16f96ab72a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/arts/30gorbachev-notebook-1/merlin_186188976_972459c5-3ee0-430e-ae05-3a16f96ab72a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/arts/30gorbachev-notebook-1/merlin_186188976_972459c5-3ee0-430e-ae05-3a16f96ab72a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/arts/30gorbachev-notebook-1/30gorbachev-notebook-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/01/arts/30gorbachev-notebook-1/30gorbachev-notebook-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/arts/30gorbachev-notebook-1/30gorbachev-notebook-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Human Most of All: In Moscow, a Theater Stages ‘Gorbachev’', 'kicker': 'Reporter’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorbachev, Mikhail S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hermanis, Alvis (1965- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Gorbachev (Play)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Theater of Nations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-30T18:47:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ivan Nechepurenko', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ivan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nechepurenko', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efaa4f4b-fa2d-585e-8df2-bd03f31de58d', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efaa4f4b-fa2d-585e-8df2-bd03f31de58d'}, {'abstract': 'A panel of experts advising the C.D.C. also discussed data showing that the Pfizer and Moderna vaccines bring a small risk of heart problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/30/health/pfizer-moderna-vaccine-myocarditis.html', 'snippet': 'A panel of experts advising the C.D.C. also discussed data showing that the Pfizer and Moderna vaccines bring a small risk of heart problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New data presented to a Centers for Disease Control and Prevention committee provided more evidence that the Covid-19 vaccines provided robust protection against severe disease through July, after the Delta variant of the coronavirus had spread widely through the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1427, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2/30virus-briefing-ACIP-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New data confirm Covid vaccines provide strong protection against hospitalization.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Data Confirm Covid-19 Vaccines Still Provide Strong Protection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Risks and Safety Concerns', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heart', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moderna Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pfizer Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-30T18:55:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Anthes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anthes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a805a0cb-2705-5e5f-8c6c-4a4ad4b24feb', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a805a0cb-2705-5e5f-8c6c-4a4ad4b24feb'}, {'abstract': 'The new media obsession with moderate minorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/30/opinion/silent-majority-white-media.html', 'snippet': 'The new media obsession with moderate minorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her 1990 book “Fear of Falling,” Barbara Ehrenreich detailed how the widely broadcast violence at the 1968 Democratic National Convention in Chicago led to an immediate, dramatic paradigm shift in media coverage. In the month before the event, Mayor Richard Daley had denounced the various anti-Vietnam War protest groups who were planning to converge outside the city’s International Amphitheater. When those protesters arrived, Daley fought back with his police force who, on Aug. 28, attacked protesters in Grant Park.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30kang/30kang-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30kang/30kang-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30kang/30kang-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30kang/30kang-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1080, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30kang/30kang-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30kang/30kang-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30kang/30kang-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the ‘Silent Majority’ Isn’t White', 'kicker': 'Jay Caspian Kang', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'internal-sub-only', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Reform', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Floyd Protests (2020)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Sixties', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-30T19:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Caspian Kang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': 'Caspian', 'lastname': 'Kang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b7fb2af-fe57-5d8a-bca6-711adc4135c9', 'word_count': 2316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b7fb2af-fe57-5d8a-bca6-711adc4135c9'}, {'abstract': 'Elon Musk has put up $100 million in prize money for a way to extract carbon from the atmosphere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/30/opinion/elon-musk-prize-patent.html', 'snippet': 'Elon Musk has put up $100 million in prize money for a way to extract carbon from the atmosphere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this year, Elon Musk, the billionaire co-founder and chief executive of Tesla, promised $100 million in prizes to inventors who come up with ways to remove greenhouse gases from the atmosphere. The rewards, which will be awarded by the X Prize Foundation, are part of a cornucopia of cash that’s being dangled to induce innovation around the world. The European Innovation Council, the MacArthur Foundation, and the U.S. government through the America Competes Reauthorization Act of 2010 are among those splashing around big bucks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30coy/30coy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30coy/30coy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30coy/30coy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30coy/30coy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30coy/30coy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30coy/30coy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/30/opinion/30coy/30coy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Better, a Prize or a Patent?', 'kicker': 'Peter Coy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'internal-sub-only', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'n