cooking.html', 'snippet': 'Fanny Singer takes some liberties with her version of the classic dish, going so far as to include lettuce.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Lettuce is not typically found in a salade niçoise — it’s sacrilege,” says the writer and art critic Fanny Singer. “But I’ll sneak lettuce into every meal.” It’s a fitting act of rebellion for the daughter of the chef and restaurateur Alice Waters, the owner of Berkeley’s legendary temple to local produce, Chez Panisse. Meanwhile, Singer’s father, Stephen Singer, owns a vineyard in Sebastopol, Calif.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO/31tmag-fanny-singer-slide-7JMO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Late-Summer Gathering, Try This Spin on a Salade Niçoise', 'kicker': 'Cooking Class', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singer, Fanny (1983- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waters, Alice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chez Panisse (Berkeley, Calif, Restaurant)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-08-31T15:45:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jamie Feldmar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jamie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feldmar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d01f04bc-1172-5be5-8ab7-825a08c6c016', 'word_count': 1364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d01f04bc-1172-5be5-8ab7-825a08c6c016'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty years later, the terrorism threat from Afghanistan  hasn’t faded. And militant competition from ISIS-K has merely increased the stakes.\xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/31/opinion/biden-isis-k.html', 'snippet': 'Twenty years later, the terrorism threat from Afghanistan  hasn’t faded. And militant competition from ISIS-K has merely increased the stakes.\xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'When President Biden announced in the spring that America would withdraw its troops from Afghanistan by the fall, he spoke of terrorism threats — but never mentioned Islamic State Khorasan, or ISIS-K, the Islamic State’s affiliate in Afghanistan. In threat assessments about Afghanistan as late as April, the director of national intelligence, Avril Haines, barely brought up ISIS-K. On Aug. 20 Mr. Biden mentioned the group, in a speech on the last-minute effort to evacuate stranded U.S. citizens and vulnerable Afghans after the Taliban had overrun Afghanistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/31/opinion/31Mir2/merlin_193884708_756cde27-f77f-4eea-9fdd-efe104d51338-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/31/opinion/31Mir2/merlin_193884708_756cde27-f77f-4eea-9fdd-efe104d51338-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/31/opinion/31Mir2/merlin_193884708_756cde27-f77f-4eea-9fdd-efe104d51338-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/31/opinion/31Mir2/merlin_193884708_756cde27-f77f-4eea-9fdd-efe104d51338-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/31/opinion/31Mir2/31Mir2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thu